{"id":238729874564447,"type":"album","name":"Rift","artist":"Phish","year":1993,"weight":10,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710909.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-40c45052-9418-4aee-83c7-8ba518afae3f/mbid-40c45052-9418-4aee-83c7-8ba518afae3f-10952339166.jpg","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"MlbTI4er_uA","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/3iiHj2P7DD5omB11AtNd97","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_lbNV2Y2Ewt16DzVDOQlYpiIFr7XFSfbDI","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/phish/rift"},"desc":"Rift is the fourth studio album by the American rock band Phish, released on February 2, 1993, by Elektra Records. It is a concept album, detailing the experience of a man dreaming about the rift in his relationship with his girlfriend. Rift was recorded in September and October 1992 and produced by Barry Beckett. Rift was certified gold by the RIAA on October 15, 1997. Rift marked the second time that the band had recorded a concept album, but the first—the rock opera–styled The Man Who Stepped into Yesterday—has never been officially released. All songs were written by Trey Anastasio ."},"artist_ref":{"id":129190030013326,"name":"Phish","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Phish_2009-12-30.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":147423806094006,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":690,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":42039639412310,"type":"genre","name":"Neo-Psychedelia","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":266,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":89886331015150,"type":"genre","name":"Jazz Fusion","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":240,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":190589917177789,"type":"genre","name":"Jam Band","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":212,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":28712889142764,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jam Band","src":"musthear